    "narrative": "The core of our lineup today rests on the high-upside pairing of **Corbin Carroll** (78.75) and **Vinnie Pasquantino** (67.48). **Corbin Carroll** remains our premier offensive engine; despite the minor penalty for facing a lefty in Lodolo, his elite speed profile and optimal placement in the two-hole make him the highest-scoring asset on our board. We are also capitalizing on a significant platoon edge for **Vinnie Pasquantino**, whose projection is bolstered by a favorable 4.04 xERA matchup against Melton. Meanwhile, **Isaac Paredes** (65.97) and **Gabriel Moreno** (65.10) provide reliable stability in the heart of the order, both benefiting from the combination of soft-tossing opponents and high-leverage lineup slots that elevate their base projections.\n\nOur decision-making process for the utility and outfield spots was heavily dictated by the scarcity of stolen bases and defensive efficiency. **Henry Bolte** (56.01) earns the nod over **Griffin Conine** primarily due to his leadoff duties, which provide a superior path to R and SB opportunities compared to **Griffin Conine**'s lower spot in the order. The most difficult cut of the day was **Brice Turang** (44.71); he was considered for the MI spot, but he was ultimately relegated to the bench due to a daunting matchup against a pitcher of Sale's caliber, which effectively suppressed his efficiency floor. We are keeping **James Wood** on the IL for now, and while **Austin Riley** remains on the bench, his recent struggles against high-end velocity (2.09 xERA matchup) kept his score below the required threshold for active rotation.\n\nWe are monitoring the weather closely, as several of our starters are facing matchups that hinge on favorable park factors; **Mickey Moniak** (53.26) and **Travis Bazzana** (49.88) are specifically riding high-park-factor boosts today that keep them relevant despite questionable platoon splits. **Jose Caballero** (54.20) represents our primary SB-chasing gamble in the eight-hole. While his SP skill penalty against Fluharty is concerning, his aggressive base-running profile remains essential as we grind through the late-season standings. Ensure all roster locks are finalized early, as we have minimal exposure to the late-game slate today.",
